Training data sources, by share of the NL->command pair pool:

  58.2%  NL2SH-ALFA training split   MIT
         https://huggingface.co/datasets/westenfelder/NL2SH-ALFA
  41.8%  tldr-pages                  CC-BY-4.0
         https://github.com/tldr-pages/tldr

Attribution, required by CC-BY-4.0: this work includes content from
tldr-pages (https://github.com/tldr-pages/tldr) under CC-BY-4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Page content is CC-BY-4.0;
only that repository's scripts/ directory is MIT.

The natural-language side of every pair was machine-translated into Bahasa
Melayu (formal, colloquial, and rojak registers) with
Gemma-SEA-LION-v3-9B-IT (https://huggingface.co/aisingapore/Gemma-SEA-LION-v3-9B-IT-GGUF),
run locally. Commands are byte-identical to their sources and were never
translated. SEA-LION inherits the Gemma Terms of Use; those terms govern the
translation model, not the translated text.

The safety checker design and the training recipe follow
ThorOdinson246/whatisit-nl2sh (Apache-2.0),
https://github.com/ThorOdinson246/whatisit-nl2sh.
